class:: BeatBandRatio
summary:: Beat-synchronous spectral band fractions
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
Accumulates squared FFT magnitudes during each beat interval, dividing each band sum by whole-spectrum energy. Shared boundary bins are counted once; uncovered frequencies make the sum less than one. Frames are assigned by their arrival time, with FFT latency retained.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: chain
FFT chain. Match fftSize and hop to FFT.

argument:: beat
Control-rate beat trigger. Each rising edge completes the preceding interval and begins a new one.

argument:: boundaries
Strictly increasing frequency boundaries in Hz, defining 1–64 bands. Default [0, 200, 800, 3200, 20000].

argument:: fftSize
FFT size, a power of two from 256–8192. Default 2048 for beat trackers and 1024 for BeatBandRatio.

argument:: maxInterval
Maximum beat interval in seconds, clipped to 0.1–60, default 10. Expired results reset to zero.

returns::
An Array of band energy fractions, initially zero until a complete interval.

examples::
BeatBandRatio accumulates squared FFT magnitudes across configurable frequency subbands during each beat interval, reporting the energy fraction of each subband at every new beat. In this example, it drives an automatic tilt EQ balancer: when low-frequency kick drums dominate the interval energy, high frequencies receive an adaptive presence boost. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: tracks the low-band energy fraction.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var bands = BeatBandRatio.kr(chain, onset[0], boundaries: [0, 250, 1500, 8000, 20000], fftSize: 1024);
        var lowRatio = bands[0].lag(0.04);
        var highBoost = BHiShelf.ar(source, 3500, 1.0, lowRatio.linlin(0.1, 0.7, 0, 8));
        var sound = (source * 0.15) + (highBoost * 0.2);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, bands[0]) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Low Band Energy Fraction", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

